# docs.rules
# The `docs` area is the one area the house engineering standards do not
# cover — the ql-docs workflow has no documentation checklist — so
# these few rules stand on their own rather than duplicating a standard.
# Every other area is governed by `<area>.standards`; see rules/_common.rules.
version: 2

## MUST
- No broken relative links to files that do not exist in the repository.
- Code samples are syntactically valid for the language they claim to be.
- No secrets, API keys, or internal-only URLs and hostnames used as examples.

## SHOULD
- Behaviour changes in code are reflected in the documentation that describes them, in the same PR.
- Documentation states what is *not* covered or not yet true, rather than implying completeness it does not have.
